THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

This repository distributes no third-party code. It references the components below by
package name or image tag, and they are fetched at install time under their own licences.
Two of them carry obligations worth reading before you deploy or redistribute.

ParadeDB / pg_search — AGPL-3.0
    The database image (paradedb/paradedb) provides both pgvector and the BM25 index this
    project's lexical half can use. It runs as a separate process, reached over the wire,
    and no part of it is included here — so its copyleft does not extend to this project's
    own code. Anyone who redistributes a bundled image, or modifies ParadeDB itself, takes
    on ParadeDB's obligations rather than these.

Hugging Face text-embeddings-inference (TEI) — HFOIL 1.0, NOT AN OPEN SOURCE LICENCE
    The embedding and reranking servers run this image. HFOIL permits internal and
    commercial use, and forbids offering TEI itself as a hosted or managed paid service
    without a separate agreement with Hugging Face. This is the only component in the stack
    that is not open source. If you intend to sell a hosted service built on this project,
    read that licence first, or replace TEI with any server exposing the same embedding API.

BAAI/bge-m3 — MIT
    The embedding model. 1024 dimensions, multilingual.

BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3 — Apache-2.0
    The cross-encoder used for reranking. Optional at runtime: its absence degrades recall
    visibly rather than failing.

psycopg, psycopg-binary, psycopg-pool, psycopg2-binary — LGPL-3.0
    Imported unmodified as libraries and replaceable, which is what makes them compatible
    with an Apache-2.0 application.

certifi — MPL-2.0
    File-level copyleft on an unmodified dependency.

Python and npm dependency closures
    Predominantly MIT, ISC, BSD and Apache-2.0. `scripts/check-licences.sh` fails the build
    on any GPL, AGPL or non-commercial licence entering the shipped Python closure; it has
    no npm equivalent. Fonts arrive as @fontsource packages under OFL-1.1 and are not
    vendored here.
